## Why This Is Asked
Assesses fundamental observability for SAP HANA on AWS, translating SAP metrics into CloudWatch and triggering actionable alerts.

## Key Concepts
- CloudWatch agent for EC2
- CloudWatch dashboards and alarms
- SNS-based alerting
- Minimal IaC (CDK/CFN)

## Code Example
```javascript
// AWS CDK snippet: creates an SNS topic and a CloudWatch alarm for EC2 CPU
const topic = new sns.Topic(this, 'SAPCpuAlarmTopic');
const alarm = new cloudwatch.Alarm(this, 'SAPCpuAlarm', {
  metric: new cloudwatch.Metric({
    namespace: 'AWS/EC2',
    metricName: 'CPUUtilization',
    dimensions: { InstanceId: 'i-0123456789abcdef0' },
  }),
  threshold: 85,
  evaluationPeriods: 1,
  datapointsToAlarm: 1,
  statistic: 'Average',
  treatMissingData: cloudwatch.TreatMissingData.NOT_SET,
});
alarm.addAlarmAction(new actions.SnsAction(topic));
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this to multi-AZ SAP HANA HA?
- How would you incorporate SAP-specific metrics without agent exposure?
- How would you tune alerts to avoid noise?

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates practical data protection across SAP on AWS with Snowflake analytics, balancing real-time access and compliance.

## Key Concepts
- SAP S/4HANA data ingestion and masking
- Field-level masking rules for PII
- Snowflake masking policies and data sharing
- AWS KMS key management and IAM governance
- Auditing, rollback, and failover strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example masking function
function maskPII(record) {
  const r = {...record};
  if (r.email) r.email = r.email.replace(/(.{2}).+(@.*)/, '$1***$2');
  if (r.phone) r.phone = r.phone.replace(/(\d{3})\d{4}(\d{3})/, '$1***$2');
  if (r.ssn) r.ssn = '***-**-' + r.ssn.slice(-4);
  return r;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate masking without leaking data in logs?
- How would you rotate keys and propagate policy changes across Snowflake without downtime?

## Why This Is Asked

